# odd-one-out — line endings are decided by the repository, not by the machine.
#
# WHY. Without this, every checkout uses whatever core.autocrlf the local git
# happens to have. This repository was written on Windows with autocrlf=true:
# the blobs are LF, but a checkout here rewrites them to CRLF, and a checkout
# elsewhere may not. The result is the same file with two different endings
# depending on who cloned it — and a diff that shows every line as changed the
# first time somebody edits it.
#
# text=auto  — git decides what is text and normalises it to LF in the repo
# eol=lf     — and writes LF on checkout, on every platform
* text=auto eol=lf
